# Income Inequality and Housing Unaffordability in the Netherlands

## How to reproduce this analysis

### Step 1 - Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/toms-kelderis/Tutorial-4-1-Income-inequality-and-housing-affordability

### Step 2 - Install R and RStudio
Download R from https://cran.r-project.org
Download RStudio from https://posit.co/download/rstudio-desktop

### Step 3 - Restore packages
Open RStudio, open the project, then run in Console:
renv::restore()

### Step 4 - Run the analysis
source("run_all.R")

## Data sources
All data is downloaded automatically from CBS via the cbsodataR package.
No manual downloads are needed.

- quintile_income: CBS datasets 83220NED (2015) through 85039NED (2021)
- median_income: CBS dataset 85064NED
- renter_households: CBS dataset 82550NED

## Folder structure
- Template_Assignment.Rmd - main analysis file
- run_all.R - script to reproduce everything
- renv.lock - package versions for reproducibility
- data/ - cleaned datasets saved as .rds files